<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/1st-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gallic Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">58–50 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Gallic Wars were the campaigns of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> from 58 to 50 BCE, which brought the whole of Gaul west of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a> under Roman rule. They included expeditions across the Rhine and to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and the defeat of the great revolt under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vercingetorix">Vercingetorix</a> at Alesia in 52 BCE. Caesar's own account, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commentarii-de-bello-gallico">Commentaries on the Gallic War</a>, is the main source.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gallic-wars.jpg" alt="Gallic Wars" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lionel Royer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lionel_Royer_-_Vercingetorix_Throwing_down_His_Weapons_at_the_feet_of_Julius_Caesar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
